#!/usr/bin/env perl
use strict;
use warnings;

use Term::Maze;

our $VERSION = '0.06';

exit Term::Maze->run(@ARGV);

__END__
=head1 NAME

maze - mazes in the terminal

=head1 SYNOPSIS

    maze                          # a 40 by 20 maze
    maze --width 20 --height 8    # a small one
    maze 40 20                    # the same two numbers, bare

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Draws a maze and lets you walk it with WASD or HJKL. The screen, the keys and
the maze itself all live in L<Term::Maze>; this is the command and nothing
else. C<q> or escape quits, and the terminal is put back the way it was on
every way out.

=head1 EXIT STATUS

    0   you reached the exit, or you quit
    2   a bad option

=head1 SEE ALSO

L<Term::Maze>, L<aze>

=cut
